---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { relativeLink } from '../../utils/links';

const path = Astro.url.pathname;
---

<SiteLayout title="Deployment — Proxyglass docs" description="Deploy Proxyglass as a native systemd service or optionally as a container on Nomad.">
  <section class="docs-page wrap">
    <div class="docs-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Deployment</span>
      <h1>A small service.<br /><span>Your choice of runtime.</span></h1>
      <p>The native Go binary and systemd service are the recommended deployment. Container and Nomad support are available when they fit your platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-grid">
      <nav class="docs-toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <strong>On this page</strong>
        <a href="#native">Native install</a>
        <a href="#systemd">systemd and nginx</a>
        <a href="#container">Container / Nomad</a>
        <a href="#health">Health endpoint</a>
        <a href="#ansible">Ansible collection</a>
      </nav>
      <article class="docs-article">
        <section class="docs-section" id="native">
          <h2>Install the native binary</h2>
          <p>Build a host-native binary with <code>make build-native</code>, or cross-build the static Linux binaries with <code>make build-all</code>. Releases are designed for Linux amd64 and arm64.</p>
          <pre class="docs-code"><code>sudo ./proxyglass --install
sudoedit /etc/proxyglass/config.yml
sudo proxyglass --generate-token --config /etc/proxyglass/config.yml
sudo systemctl enable --now proxyglass</code></pre>
          <p>The installer creates the service account, config and data directories, systemd unit and <code>/etc/default/proxyglass</code>. Existing config is preserved on reinstall. Follow logs with <code>journalctl -u proxyglass -f</code>; the packaged default also writes to <code>/var/log/proxyglass/proxyglass.log</code>.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-section" id="systemd">
          <h2>systemd behind nginx</h2>
          <p>The packaged config listens on <code>127.0.0.1:8080</code>, so the dashboard is not exposed directly. nginx handles TLS and forwards <code>Host</code> plus <code>X-Forwarded-Proto</code> for OIDC.</p>
          <p>Set optional <code>HTTP_PROXY</code>, <code>HTTPS_PROXY</code> and <code>NO_PROXY</code> values in <code>/etc/default/proxyglass</code>, then restart the service.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-section" id="container">
          <h2>Container and Nomad</h2>
          <p>Build the optional image with <code>docker build -f docker/Dockerfile -t proxyglass .</code>. Mount a config file at <code>/etc/proxyglass/config.yml</code>. A sample Nomad job is provided in <code>deploy/proxyglass.nomad.hcl</code>; configure a persistent writable volume for token storage.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-section" id="health">
          <h2>Health check</h2>
          <p><code>GET /healthz</code> returns <code>200 OK</code> and <code>ok</code> for load balancer and Nomad health checks. The endpoint does not require dashboard authentication.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-section" id="ansible">
          <h2>Ansible collection</h2>
          <p>Prefer infrastructure as code? The <code>chrisvanmeer.proxyglass</code> collection installs and manages Proxyglass: it downloads the right binary for your architecture, validates the temp mount for <code>noexec</code>, deploys a default config, manages the systemd service, and generates an admin token idempotently. Downloads honour <code>HTTP_PROXY</code>/<code>HTTPS_PROXY</code>. See the <a href={relativeLink(path, '/docs/ansible')}>Ansible docs</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <nav class="docs-nav wrap" aria-label="Documentation pages">
    <a href={relativeLink(path, '/docs')}>Docs</a>
    <a href={relativeLink(path, '/docs/configuration')}>Configuration</a>
    <a href={relativeLink(path, '/docs/oidc')}>OIDC</a>
    <a href={relativeLink(path, '/docs/deployment')}>Deployment</a>
    <a href={relativeLink(path, '/docs/ansible')}>Ansible</a>
  </nav>
</SiteLayout>
